source	Thomas Aquinas, Summa Theologica I, tr. Fathers of the English Dominican Province (1920), q.2 a.3
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 17611, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/17611
class	inference
at	S8	Therefore it is necessary to admit a first efficient cause
fault	the regress premise conflates "no first cause" with "no cause at all"; and the first cause is identified with God without argument
reference	A. Kenny, The Five Ways (1969), ch. 3
known	canon
